    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Liu Che came to the throne at 15 in 141 BCE and, after the death of his grandmother Empress Dowager Dou in 135 BCE, ruled with full control of the government for the rest of a 54-year reign.</li><li>His armies drove the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiongnu-empire">Xiongnu</a> out of the Ordos Desert and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qilian-mountains">Qilian Mountains</a>, opened the way to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a> and annexed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanyue">Nanyue</a>, Dian and Gojoseon, while the cost of the wars brought new levies, famine and peasant revolts.</li><li>He promoted Confucian learning and strengthened the emperor's power over the prime minister, yet governed by harsh officials, and the witchcraft persecutions of his last years killed his own crown prince and many others.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Wu is said to have raised the Imperial Music Bureau to a prestigious institution; it collected folk songs from across the country and songs based on Central Asian tunes, and gave its name to the yuefu style of poetry.</p></aside>
    </section>

